# Unified diffs are byte-exact: git apply's context matching treats a trailing \r as
# ordinary content, not ignorable whitespace. These patches are applied against
# build/vendor/zimodem-src, which tools/Vendoring/DirectoryCopy.cs always normalizes to
# LF regardless of the submodule's own checked-out line endings (see
# docs/native-wrapper-spec.md section 6.3a) -- so the patch files themselves must also
# always check out as LF, or a machine with core.autocrlf=true (Git for Windows'
# default, including GitHub's windows-latest runners) silently corrupts them into CRLF
# on checkout and every patch fails to apply.
patches/**/*.patch text eol=lf
